Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.09,0:00:02.76,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's filled up so much.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.67,0:00:07.32,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}I see. It's because I've met \NOtome and Remnan now, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.11,0:00:09.75,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}After it fills completely...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.82,0:00:13.95,Default,SETSU,0,0,0,,And once it gets all of \Nthe knowledge it desires,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.95,0:00:18.50,Default,SETSU,0,0,0,,the Silver Key will leave its host \Nand head to another dimension
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.50,0:00:20.46,Default,SETSU,0,0,0,,to find a new host.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.22,0:00:24.13,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,I wonder how much further I have to go.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.56,0:02:01.49,Default,SIGN,0,0,0,,{\an8}EPISODE 8: GUARD DUTY
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.70,0:01:59.95,Default,SETSU,0,0,0,,Okay, let's go ahead and start \Ntoday's meeting. LeVi.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.40,0:02:02.08,Default,LEVI,0,0,0,,{\an8}{\i1}As you wish.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.30,0:02:08.56,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}In this world line, a total \Nof fifteen boarded this ship.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.99,0:02:13.23,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}And out of the fifteen, \Nthere are four Gnosia.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.46,0:02:18.62,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}During the first day's meeting, \NComet was sent into cold sleep,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.62,0:02:22.41,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}and after that, Stella was attacked \Nby the Gnosia and eliminated.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.44,0:02:24.67,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}On the second day,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.67,0:02:27.66,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}Shigemichi was chosen for \Ncold sleep during the meeting.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.00,0:02:32.49,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}After that, we lost Jonas to the Gnosia.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.97,0:02:37.49,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}Now we have eleven left,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.49,0:02:41.00,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}and we don't know how many \NGnosia remain among them.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.66,0:02:45.24,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,If I can just go over it one more time...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.24,0:02:50.93,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,We can safely assume that whoever is on \NGuard Duty is confirmed human, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.42,0:02:55.37,Default,LEVI,0,0,0,,{\i1}Affirmative. Kukrushka and Remnan
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.37,0:02:58.60,Default,LEVI,0,0,0,,{\i1}did not leave this ship while \Nwe were docked in Liu-An,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.60,0:03:01.57,Default,LEVI,0,0,0,,{\i1}so the probability that they were \Ninfected by Gnosia is zero.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.00,0:03:03.17,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.88,0:03:07.43,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}Guard Duty... The new role I found \Nout about during this loop.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.66,0:03:13.80,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}The Engineer can investigate one person per \Nday and determine if they're human or Gnosia.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.80,0:03:17.30,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}The Doctor can investigate \Nwhoever was chosen for cold sleep
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.30,0:03:21.58,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}during the previous meeting \Nand determine if they're human or Gnosia.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.93,0:03:28.27,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}The Guardian Angel can choose one person \Nto protect during the warp from Gnosia attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.57,0:03:33.76,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}And now, Guard Duty—two people \Nwho are confirmed to be human.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.28,0:03:36.82,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}It just keeps getting more \Nand more complicated.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.21,0:03:42.29,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}So, if there are up to four Gnosia \Nout of the eleven of us left,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.29,0:03:44.90,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}and two people are confirmed to be human...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.37,0:03:47.45,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,P-Please stop.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.90,0:03:51.00,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,W-We're in a meeting right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.00,0:03:52.37,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}Kukrushka...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.01,0:03:56.58,Default,YURIKO,0,0,0,,Come, now. The banquet has already begun.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.58,0:03:59.01,Default,YURIKO,0,0,0,,Hurry up and dance for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.37,0:04:03.40,Default,CHIPIE,0,0,0,,First, I'm gonna make my \Nreport as the Engineer.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.40,0:04:07.90,Default,CHIPIE,0,0,0,,I checked out Setsu, and they were a Gnosia.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.90,0:04:12.95,Default,SETSU,0,0,0,,I see. If you consider me as being in the way, \Nthat must mean that you're a Gnosia.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.95,0:04:15.09,Default,CHIPIE,0,0,0,,Of course you'd say that.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.53,0:04:18.99,Default,CHIPIE,0,0,0,,It's up to all of you to decide who \Nyou believe, but I'm the real one.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.40,0:04:21.49,Default,JINA,0,0,0,,And the Doctor's report?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.49,0:04:24.99,Default,RACIO,0,0,0,,I've already investigated \Nthe body in cold sleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.35,0:04:27.53,Default,RACIO,0,0,0,,Shigemichi was human.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.00,0:04:29.64,Default,JINA,0,0,0,,I also investigated him.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.64,0:04:31.00,Default,JINA,0,0,0,,Shigemichi was...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.00,0:04:32.26,Default,JINA,0,0,0,,a Gnosia.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.60,0:04:37.75,Default,SQ,0,0,0,,So what's going on here? \NThat, like, makes no sense.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.75,0:04:40.04,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yeah, she's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.64,0:04:43.93,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}The ones who came forward as the \NDoctor and Engineer are these four.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.32,0:04:48.01,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}Shigemichi was sent into \Ncold sleep the day before.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.65,0:04:51.85,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}And Racio says Shigemichi was human,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.85,0:04:54.16,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}while Jina says that he was Gnosia.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.59,0:04:57.61,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}Which means one of them must be lying.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.27,0:05:03.92,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}We know for sure that out of these four, \Ntwo of them are Gnosia.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.36,0:05:07.50,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}If we can confirm that \Neven one of them is lying,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.82,0:05:13.05,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}we should be able to narrow down exactly \Nwhich two are human and which two are Gnosia.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.25,0:05:17.83,Default,SHA-MING,0,0,0,,Pretty sure this is exactly the time to \Nask the wise humans what they think.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.14,0:05:19.00,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.00,0:05:24.42,Default,SHA-MING,0,0,0,,They're right there. The two \Nwho're confirmed to be human.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.85,0:05:29.14,Default,OTOME,0,0,0,,O-Of course! What do you think, Kukrushka?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.26,0:05:36.71,Default,OTOME,0,0,0,,You don't know... but... the most \Nsuspicious one to you is...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.03,0:05:42.29,Default,SHA-MING,0,0,0,,Really?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.29,0:05:45.04,Default,SHA-MING,0,0,0,,Hold up! You gotta be messed in the head!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.04,0:05:49.70,Default,OTOME,0,0,0,,She says that she has no basis for this. \NIt's just a gut feeling.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.70,0:05:54.74,Default,SETSU,0,0,0,,It may be a gut feeling, but we know \Nthat it's a {\i1}human's{\i0} gut feeling.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.29,0:05:58.45,Default,SHA-MING,0,0,0,,Whoa, whoa. Y'all are crazy.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.45,0:06:00.29,Default,SHA-MING,0,0,0,,Where's this goin'?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.27,0:06:05.82,Default,LEVI,0,0,0,,{\i1}It has been decided.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.82,0:06:09.11,Default,LEVI,0,0,0,,{\i1}Sha-ming will be put into cold sleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.11,0:06:11.06,Default,SHA-MING,0,0,0,,Seriously?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.06,0:06:15.24,Default,SQ,0,0,0,,You're the one who opened his big mouth \Nand said we should ask a human.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.24,0:06:16.70,Default,SQ,0,0,0,,Big yikes.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.09,0:06:19.80,Default,JINA,0,0,0,,But... the decision has been made.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.69,0:06:22.57,Default,SHA-MING,0,0,0,,Are you for real?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.18,0:06:27.44,Default,SHA-MING,0,0,0,,Heh, then I've got somethin' \Nup my sleeve, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.74,0:06:31.23,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,What is it? I didn't say any...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.26,0:06:40.92,Default,SHA-MING,0,0,0,,I'm so sorry!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.12,0:06:43.42,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,He's groveling?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.42,0:06:44.89,Default,CHIPIE,0,0,0,,First time I've seen this in real life.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.18,0:06:49.58,Default,SQ,0,0,0,,I can't help but want to step on him.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.38,0:06:55.07,Default,SHA-MING,0,0,0,,I got cocky! I'll reflect upon my actions! \NI'll change my ways!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.07,0:06:56.63,Default,SHA-MING,0,0,0,,So just this once! Please!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.63,0:07:00.24,Default,SHA-MING,0,0,0,,Let me go just this once! \NPlease, just this once!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.53,0:07:01.57,Default,SHA-MING,0,0,0,,Please?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.22,0:07:05.50,Default,SETSU,0,0,0,,Sorry, but we can't.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.96,0:07:10.24,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,But... Kukrushka did say that it \Nwas a baseless gut feeling, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.58,0:07:15.26,Default,RACIO,0,0,0,,Well, it is true that I'd prefer \Nto employ a more objective approach.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.74,0:07:17.24,Default,YURIKO,0,0,0,,Lowly scum.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.24,0:07:20.38,Default,YURIKO,0,0,0,,I couldn't care less what happens \Nto someone so insignificant.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.67,0:07:22.47,Default,YURIKO,0,0,0,,Do as you please.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.34,0:07:27.85,Default,SHA-MING,0,0,0,,{\an8}Woo!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.20,0:07:30.36,Default,SHA-MING,0,0,0,,Ain't this great?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.36,0:07:34.29,Default,SHA-MING,0,0,0,,So yeah, see you folks tomorrow!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.84,0:07:36.47,Default,SETSU,0,0,0,,But why...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.47,0:07:37.84,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,Do you have a problem with this?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.84,0:07:39.34,Default,SETSU,0,0,0,,Of course I do!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.34,0:07:42.23,Default,SETSU,0,0,0,,Each meeting, we choose one person \Nto send into cold sleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.23,0:07:44.44,Default,SETSU,0,0,0,,That's our agreement with LeVi.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.44,0:07:46.47,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,It is,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.47,0:07:50.03,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,but we did end up choosing someone \Nfor a pretty sketchy reason.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.03,0:07:54.02,Default,SETSU,0,0,0,,If we start saying things like that, \Nit invalidates the whole meeting process.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.02,0:07:56.83,Default,SETSU,0,0,0,,Without a rule-based order, \Nthere can only be chaos.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.83,0:07:58.05,Default,SETSU,0,0,0,,And then...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.44,0:08:00.81,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,We'll just go back.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.31,0:08:05.78,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,At the very least, that's the case \Nfor you and me, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.19,0:08:12.77,Default,SETSU,0,0,0,,But for everyone else, this is \Ntheir one and only world line.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.33,0:08:14.90,Default,SETSU,0,0,0,,This is all they get.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.97,0:08:19.16,Default,SETSU,0,0,0,,It's disrespectful to them \Nto only consider the "next time."
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.88,0:08:20.94,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,Sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.47,0:08:22.99,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,You're totally right.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.52,0:08:26.75,Default,SETSU,0,0,0,,Though this might just be \Nmy own stubbornness speaking.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.75,0:08:29.19,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,That's what's great about you, Setsu.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.19,0:08:31.66,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,No matter the world line, \Nyou're always serious.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.12,0:08:35.41,Default,SETSU,0,0,0,,That doesn't really sound like a compliment.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.73,0:08:39.67,Default,SETSU,0,0,0,,But I'll say the same thing \Nright back to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.69,0:08:47.25,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}I can't deny what Setsu said.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.25,0:08:50.75,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}I need to do my best for everyone's sake.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.14,0:08:56.18,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,Remnan...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.18,0:08:59.97,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,Um... can you spare a minute?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.11,0:09:02.22,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,Sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.69,0:09:06.03,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,Kukrushka?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.40,0:09:09.65,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,Yes. She insists on staying by my side.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.09,0:09:13.50,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,The two of you on Guard Duty \Nare the only confirmed humans.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.50,0:09:15.12,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,I'm sure she just trusts you.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.66,0:09:17.37,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,Do you think so?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.87,0:09:19.53,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,Is there something on your mind?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.98,0:09:20.97,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,Not really.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.38,0:09:23.83,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,It's just, I can't handle them.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.83,0:09:26.91,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,I can't handle mysterious women like her.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.91,0:09:29.60,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,You're scared of her? But she's just a girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.60,0:09:31.71,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,And she's so small.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.13,0:09:33.28,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.28,0:09:37.43,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,But when she looks at me with those eyes,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.30,0:09:39.78,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,my hands start to...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.22,0:09:47.30,Default,OTOME,0,0,0,,Oh, Kukrushka. You say the wildest things.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.23,0:09:51.20,Default,OTOME,0,0,0,,I-I can't breathe from laughing so hard.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.48,0:09:52.86,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,What are you doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.86,0:09:58.04,Default,OTOME,0,0,0,,Oh, Yuri! Kukrushka keeps \Ntelling me the funniest stories.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.04,0:09:59.54,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,Stories?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.54,0:10:03.68,Default,OTOME,0,0,0,,Kukrushka uses gestures to speak.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.18,0:10:08.76,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,What is she saying?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.76,0:10:11.07,Default,OTOME,0,0,0,,She wants to play with him.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.56,0:10:18.30,Default,OTOME,0,0,0,,It's so pretty.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.30,0:10:21.06,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,Is this your first time \Nseeing scenery like this?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.06,0:10:24.73,Default,OTOME,0,0,0,,Oh, no. Dr. Yoshikado has taught me so much.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.73,0:10:28.06,Default,OTOME,0,0,0,,But this is my first time \Nseeing this in person,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.06,0:10:31.77,Default,OTOME,0,0,0,,because I'm from a sea planet.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.36,0:10:33.78,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.80,0:10:41.49,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,This...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.49,0:10:43.83,Default,OTOME,0,0,0,,She's saying you can have it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.92,0:10:46.07,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,This is...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.79,0:10:52.05,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,Thorns?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.38,0:10:58.73,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,No... No!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.45,0:11:02.65,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.40,0:11:14.92,Default,OTOME,0,0,0,,Are you all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.83,0:11:29.89,Default,YURIKO,0,0,0,,{\an8}Does that thing actually look human to you?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.22,0:11:31.59,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,"That thing"?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.59,0:11:33.22,Default,YURIKO,0,0,0,,Kukrushka.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.74,0:11:35.96,Default,YURIKO,0,0,0,,Under the stars' gaze, all is laid bare.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.96,0:11:39.43,Default,YURIKO,0,0,0,,She's no Gnosia, either. She's something...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.06,0:11:41.27,Default,YURIKO,0,0,0,,different.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.60,0:11:42.81,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,"Different"?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.45,0:11:48.20,Default,YURIKO,0,0,0,,If you let her outer beauty beguile you...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.20,0:11:50.70,Default,YURIKO,0,0,0,,you will lose sight of the truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.91,0:11:56.98,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}What could all this mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.98,0:12:00.79,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}Kukrushka should be human in this world line. \NThat's the one thing we know for sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.05,0:12:14.85,Default,LEVI,0,0,0,,{\i1}I do not sense Yuriko's presence.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.85,0:12:16.56,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,So Yuriko was...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.56,0:12:18.27,Default,RACIO,0,0,0,,Well, from the Gnosia's perspective,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.27,0:12:20.57,Default,RACIO,0,0,0,,she was the second greatest \Nthreat to them after me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.57,0:12:24.86,Default,RACIO,0,0,0,,The fact that the Guardian Angel failed to \Nprotect her shows just how useless they are.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.86,0:12:27.26,Default,RACIO,0,0,0,,It's safe to say we can't rely on them.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.58,0:12:30.01,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}The Gnosia only attack humans.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.86,0:12:33.43,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}Which means that the three \Nattacked by the Gnosia—
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.43,0:12:36.67,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}Stella, Jonas, and Yuriko—\Nare confirmed human.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.67,0:12:39.34,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}Kukrushka and Remnan, \Nwho were on Guard Duty,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.34,0:12:42.23,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}are also confirmed human, \Nand I can rule out myself, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.23,0:12:46.34,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}Which means that the four Gnosia \Nmust be among the remaining nine.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.51,0:12:50.44,Default,CHIPIE,0,0,0,,All right. I'm gonna go ahead \Nand make today's report.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.44,0:12:51.17,Default,CHIPIE,0,0,0,,Yesterday—
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.17,0:12:53.59,Default,RACIO,0,0,0,,Before you go any further, \NI have a proposal to make.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.59,0:12:56.42,Default,RACIO,0,0,0,,We should send Chipie into cold sleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.72,0:12:59.35,Default,SQ,0,0,0,,Ooh? That escalated quickly!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.35,0:13:01.91,Default,CHIPIE,0,0,0,,Of course you'd say that.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.30,0:13:06.96,Default,CHIPIE,0,0,0,,You've already reported that Shigemichi, \Nwho claimed Engineer, was human,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.96,0:13:09.19,Default,CHIPIE,0,0,0,,so from your perspective I can only be Gnosia.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.85,0:13:12.58,Default,RACIO,0,0,0,,You are precisely correct. However...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.58,0:13:15.24,Default,RACIO,0,0,0,,Even if I happened to be lying,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.24,0:13:19.03,Default,RACIO,0,0,0,,freezing you would be far more \Nadvantageous for the humans.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.31,0:13:21.79,Default,SQ,0,0,0,,You got it, Professor Racio!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.79,0:13:26.54,Default,SQ,0,0,0,,So basically, if we put you both in the fridge, \Nwhichever of you it is, we win!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.54,0:13:28.86,Default,RACIO,0,0,0,,Simply put, yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.86,0:13:30.87,Default,CHIPIE,0,0,0,,That's a bit bloodthirsty.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.87,0:13:32.76,Default,CHIPIE,0,0,0,,Are you all okay with this?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.76,0:13:35.58,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,Sorry, but I agree.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.58,0:13:36.63,Default,CHIPIE,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.63,0:13:40.68,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,Of course, I'll feel bad if you end up \Nbeing the real Engineer, Chipie.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.68,0:13:44.02,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,But Shigemichi, the other one \Nclaiming Engineer,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.33,0:13:48.01,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,was put into cold sleep very early this time.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.01,0:13:50.53,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,You're the only Engineer left.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.53,0:13:55.28,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,If you happened to be Gnosia, you'd have \Nfree rein to manipulate all the information.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.85,0:13:56.82,Default,CHIPIE,0,0,0,,"This time"?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.90,0:13:58.83,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,Er...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.83,0:14:03.25,Default,SHA-MING,0,0,0,,Heh. Dead men tell no tales. Understand?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.58,0:14:06.44,Default,OTOME,0,0,0,,But I really do feel bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.44,0:14:08.70,Default,CHIPIE,0,0,0,,Otome... Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.70,0:14:10.81,Default,CHIPIE,0,0,0,,This is totally unfair!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.81,0:14:13.78,Default,JINA,0,0,0,,I agree. There's no actual \Nreason to suspect him.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.78,0:14:15.64,Default,SETSU,0,0,0,,I get what you're saying, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.24,0:14:17.84,Default,CHIPIE,0,0,0,,All right, fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.27,0:14:22.85,Default,CHIPIE,0,0,0,,Then let me off the hook just this once, \Nlike you did for Sha-ming yesterday.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.44,0:14:25.17,Default,SETSU,0,0,0,,Huh? But that's...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.62,0:14:28.81,Default,CHIPIE,0,0,0,,You're not going to let Sha-ming \Nget special treatment, are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.50,0:14:33.65,Default,SHA-MING,0,0,0,,Ooh, your angry face is excellent, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.27,0:14:35.86,Default,OTOME,0,0,0,,Excuse me...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.24,0:14:39.81,Default,OTOME,0,0,0,,Kukrushka says she knows \Na good way to deal with this.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.71,0:14:44.12,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,Send everyone into cold sleep?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.12,0:14:44.75,Default,OTOME,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.17,0:14:50.88,Default,OTOME,0,0,0,,She's suggesting that since she \Nand Remnan are confirmed human,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.88,0:14:55.33,Default,OTOME,0,0,0,,they can look after the ship while \Nthe rest of us go into cold sleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.33,0:14:57.55,Default,SQ,0,0,0,,Isn't that a bit heavy-handed?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.55,0:15:00.13,Default,RACIO,0,0,0,,But it makes perfect sense.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.13,0:15:06.34,Default,RACIO,0,0,0,,This is the one way we can ensure that every \NGnosia infectee is sent into cold sleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.71,0:15:08.41,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,What do you think, Setsu?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.41,0:15:11.26,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,We'd be breaking our agreement \Nwith LeVi again, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.61,0:15:15.81,Default,SETSU,0,0,0,,Well, unlike the groveling, \Nthis makes logical sense.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.81,0:15:18.87,Default,SETSU,0,0,0,,The two who'll remain have been \Nconfirmed to be human, so...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.73,0:15:22.65,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,I... don't like this idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.01,0:15:25.32,Default,CHIPIE,0,0,0,,What? You're actually against this?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.32,0:15:27.70,Default,CHIPIE,0,0,0,,Then we should probably \Ncall it off, shouldn't we?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.70,0:15:31.58,Default,SHA-MING,0,0,0,,You're gettin' frozen either way, pal.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.58,0:15:35.59,Default,CHIPIE,0,0,0,,If we're gonna go down that road, you should \Nprobably get frozen, too, shouldn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.86,0:15:38.63,Default,SHA-MING,0,0,0,,Why, though? Man, you're annoyin'.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.63,0:15:41.95,Default,SHA-MING,0,0,0,,You oughta let your cat \Ndo the talkin' instead.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.60,0:15:46.58,Default,SETSU,0,0,0,,Remnan... Could you please agree to this?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.58,0:15:47.73,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,Setsu...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.35,0:15:54.40,Default,SETSU,0,0,0,,This is on all of us for breaking the rules \Nyesterday and letting Sha-ming go.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.40,0:15:58.26,Default,SETSU,0,0,0,,There's no other way \Nto restore order at this point.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.99,0:16:00.60,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,All right...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.33,0:16:11.24,Default,SQ,0,0,0,,Man, I hate cold sleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.24,0:16:15.04,Default,SHA-MING,0,0,0,,Goin' beddy-bye in this thing not knowin' \Nwhen or if you might wake up again
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.04,0:16:16.85,Default,SHA-MING,0,0,0,,is super harsh.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.61,0:16:20.01,Default,SETSU,0,0,0,,I haven't seen things \Nplay out this way before.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.01,0:16:23.23,Default,SETSU,0,0,0,,This might be the most \Npeaceful resolution yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.63,0:16:25.92,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,I wonder if this will change anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.57,0:16:27.88,Default,SETSU,0,0,0,,Who knows?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.88,0:16:31.48,Default,SETSU,0,0,0,,I'm pretty sure that you and I \Nwill loop again, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.23,0:16:34.40,Default,SETSU,0,0,0,,Well... see you again.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.98,0:16:42.03,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}I wonder how many more times \NI'm going to have to repeat this.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.74,0:17:02.33,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,Wake up! Please wake up!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.61,0:17:04.84,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,Yuri! Yuri!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.48,0:17:06.32,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,Remnan...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.32,0:17:08.56,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,Hurry! Please! Hurry up and move!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.56,0:17:09.21,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.02,0:17:19.68,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,SQ...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.68,0:17:21.53,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,Hurry! She's coming!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.53,0:17:24.10,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,She's coming back here for sure!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.10,0:17:25.19,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,So please...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.19,0:17:27.24,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\an8}Coming back here? What is—
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.72,0:17:30.66,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,Remnan!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.96,0:17:44.55,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,Kukrushka...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.05,0:17:52.34,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,Setsu!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.07,0:18:22.29,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,LeVi!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.29,0:18:25.55,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,Lock down the lower level and \Nthe cold sleep room immediately!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.55,0:18:29.92,Default,LEVI,0,0,0,,{\i1}Emergency. Emergen... E-E-E...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.92,0:18:34.11,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,LeVi! Lock it down! \NActivate the security doors!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.11,0:18:34.76,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,LeVi!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.81,0:18:39.90,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}Does this mean... \NLeVi's already been neutralized, too?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.94,0:18:45.40,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,Sha-ming...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.94,0:18:50.91,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}Was Kukrushka a Gnosia?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.41,0:18:54.24,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}No... since she was on Guard Duty, \Nshe should be human.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.72,0:18:57.77,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}Not to mention, the Gnosia \Nwouldn't do something this overt.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.14,0:19:00.27,Default,JINA,0,0,0,,Yuri!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.34,0:19:02.46,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,Jina!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.46,0:19:06.03,Default,JINA,0,0,0,,I can't get ahold of LeVi. \NYou should escape outside, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.03,0:19:07.30,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,Outside?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.30,0:19:11.26,Default,JINA,0,0,0,,Out here, we can still barely \Nsend an SOS to Liu-An.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.26,0:19:12.62,Default,JINA,0,0,0,,I'll open the airlock.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.28,0:19:20.69,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,Don't open it! Just head \Nout there without me, Jina!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.69,0:19:22.18,Default,JINA,0,0,0,,Huh? But...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.18,0:19:26.01,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,I'll use the escape pod upstairs \Nand come and get you!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.01,0:19:27.40,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,So hurry!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.42,0:19:34.66,Default,JINA,0,0,0,,H-Hurry... Hurry...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.66,0:19:36.96,Default,COMPUTER VOICE,0,0,0,,{\i1}Commence emergency opening.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.01,0:19:55.28,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,Jina!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.97,0:20:02.65,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,{\i1}Jina... Setsu... SQ... Everyone...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.69,0:20:08.64,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,Y-Yuri!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.89,0:20:10.03,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,Hurry!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.84,0:20:17.50,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,What in the world happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.50,0:20:19.27,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.27,0:20:21.99,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,A-As soon as we were alone together,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.99,0:20:26.07,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,Kukrushka suddenly went up to everyone \Nwho was in cold sleep and...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.49,0:20:30.31,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,Is that Kukrushka... really Kukrushka?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.31,0:20:31.68,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.10,0:20:33.33,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,It's just...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.33,0:20:34.84,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,Just...?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.84,0:20:41.05,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,I used to be someone \Nelse's property. Someone's pet.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.66,0:20:42.81,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,"Pet"?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.81,0:20:45.81,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,Yes. Every day was hell.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.61,0:20:48.72,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,She made me wear a control \Ncollar around my neck,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.27,0:20:51.90,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,and I couldn't do anything \Nwithout her permission.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.54,0:20:55.61,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,That's why I desperately ran away.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.61,0:20:59.11,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,I ran to the far reaches of space!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.39,0:21:04.06,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,But no matter how far I ran, \Nno matter how many decades I hid...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.06,0:21:07.07,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,She... She still comes after me!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.07,0:21:09.24,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,Just so she can toy with me again!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.47,0:21:12.57,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,So you're saying...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.57,0:21:15.01,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,the one who kept you as \Na pet was... Kukrushka?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.01,0:21:19.17,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,No. But... she's the same!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.45,0:21:21.18,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,The way her eyes look at me!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.48,0:21:23.18,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,The way she smiles!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.67,0:21:26.23,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,I just can't anymore!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.61,0:21:31.19,Default,POD VOICE,0,0,0,,{\i1}{\an8}Launching in ten, nine, eight, seven,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.19,0:21:37.18,Default,POD VOICE,0,0,0,,{\i1}{\an8}six, five, four, three, two, one...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.18,0:21:39.22,Default,POD VOICE,0,0,0,,{\i1}{\an8}one... one...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.22,0:21:42.90,Default,POD VOICE,0,0,0,,{\i1}{\an8}one... one... one... one... one...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.10,0:21:41.31,Default,REMNAN,0,0,0,,Why...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:10.22,0:22:12.77,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,Did I... loop?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:14.20,0:22:15.52,Default,YURI,0,0,0,,What's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:24.70,0:22:28.58,Default,COMET,0,0,0,,Welcome to the world of the Gnosia!

